     "stdout": "\nHaze in Singapore: PSI back to ‘unhealthy’ range in all regions; PM2.5 enters ‘high’ range in the west - Yahoo News Singapore https://sg.news.yahoo.com/haze-singapore-psi-back-unhealthy-230732779.html 0 days ago\nSingapore is in its 13th consecutive day of unhealthy air since Oct 5 – the longest continuous stretch of poor air quality the country has endured since the 2015 haze crisis. That year, bad air lasted 14 days from Sept 23 to Oct 7. In its ...\n\n# Haze in Singapore: PSI back to ‘unhealthy’ range in all regions; PM2.5 enters ‘high’ range in the west\nSINGAPORE – The hazy conditions continued in the morning of Oct 17 even as the 24-hour PSI in central Singapore dipped back to the \"unhealthy\" band after staying in the \"very unhealthy\" range the day before.\n\nAt 11am, the 24-hour PSI was in the \"unhealthy\" range in all regions: central (184), north (139), south (154), east (174), west (176).\n\nThe central region was worst hit on Oct 16 when the 24-hour PSI there registered \"very unhealthy\" readings throughout the day, peaking at a season high of 229 from 3pm to 4pm, till the early hours of Oct 17.\n\n\n\nAir quality is considered \"unhealthy\" when the PSI – a 24-hour rolling average of six key air pollutants – is in the range of 101 to 200, and \"very unhealthy\" when it is in the range of 201 to 300.\n\nIn its daily haze advisory on the evening of Oct 16, the National Environment Agency (NEA) said \n---\nThe National Environment Agency https://www.nea.gov.sg/ 8 days ago\nEnvironment-related information such as weather, air quality (1-hr PM2.5 readings), dengue, hawker centres, recycling and others in Singapore.\n\nEnvironment-related information such as weather, air quality (1-hr PM2.5 readings), dengue, hawker centres, recycling and others in Singapore.\n\n## Today's air quality at\n24-hr PSI\n\n1-hr PM2.5 (µg/m^3)\n\n## What's New\n### Advisory\n\n16 Oct 2026\n\n### Haze Situation Update (16 October 2026)\n\nSingapore, 16 October 2026 – The PSI forecast for 17 Oct 2026 is 150 &ndas...\n---\nHaze situation - NEA Weather https://neaweather.com/haze None\nHotspots, 24-hour PSI and the southwest-monsoon haze window.\n\n# Haze situation\n## Air Quality\n### 1-hr PM2.5\nHighest of the 5 regions (west)\n\n158\n\nNEA summary: PSI Forecast: 150 - 230 Unhealthy to Very Unhealthy\n\n## Current Haze Situation\n### Health Advisory\nIf Elevated PM2.5, avoid strenuous outdoor activity for the next hour.  Persons with chronic lung/heart disease: PSI Forecast-Unhealthy to Very Unhealthy. To plan for 17 Oct, avoid outdoor activity. For immediate outdoor activities, use 1h PM2.5.\n\n## Major Haze Episodes Affecting Singapore\nPSI values shown are the peak 24-hour national readings reported by NEA during each episode. The worst episodes typically coincide with strong El Niño years and prolonged dry spells over southern Sumatra and Kalimantan.\n\n## Haze is almost never local\nThree checks: 1-hour PM2.5 for the earliest move, 24-hour PSI for the official advisory, hotspot counts for a warning a day or two out. Haze ends when it rains on the fires or the wind turns.\n---\nwww.malaymail.com https://www.malaymail.com/news/world/2015/09/15/singapore-air-quality-remains-at-unhealthy-level/970085 None\nSINGAPORE, Sept 15 — The current hazy condition persists in Singapore, with the air quality continuing to stay at an unhealthy level.\n\nThe National Environment Agency (NEA) said today, the prevailing winds are forecast to blow from the southwest, and the current hazy conditions are expected to persist.\n\nAs of 8am today, the 24-hour pollutant standard index (PSI) stood at 122 - 150, and the three-hour PSI at 114.\n\nA 24-hour PSI reading of above 100 indicates unhealthy air quality.\n\nThe haze situation could further deteriorate should the current unfavourable winds blow in denser haze from Sumatra.\n\nThundery showers are forecast for Singapore in early morning hours, but this may only bring a brief temporary respite to the hazy conditions. — Bernama\n---\nwww.malaymail.com https://www.malaymail.com/amp/news/world/2015/10/24/singapore-air-quality-enters-very-unhealthy-range/992887 None\nWorld\nSingapore air quality enters very unhealthy range\nThe Singapore haze as seen in Sengkang at 6.45am on Oct 24, 2015. u00e2u20acu201d TODAY pic\n\nSINGAPORE, Oct 24 — Hazy conditions on the island worsened this morning. Air quality entered the very healthy range at 4am, and the 24-hour PSI had climbed since.\n\nAt 11am, the 24-hour PSI is in the 186-229 range. The three-hour PSI is at 178, down from 1am’s 232.\n\nYesterday, the National Environment Agency (NEA) said the hazy conditions are expected to continue today, with the 24-hour Pollutant Standards Index (PSI) for the next 24 hours is expected to be in the mid to high sections of the unhealthy range over the next 24 hours, and may enter the low end of the very unhealthy range if denser haze is blown in.\n\nReduced visibility is also expected to persist.\n\nThe NEA said that some haze from Kalimantan had spread to the surrounding region, and was being blown in by the prevailing south-easterly winds.\n---\n",
